# Line-ending policy.
#
# `instruction-manuals/` holds the DISTRIBUTED copies of the master instruction
# manuals published by the upstream project. They must stay byte-identical to
# their master source and are verified with SHA-256 (procedure in that
# directory's README). Automatic line-ending conversion would silently break
# that contract on any machine with `core.autocrlf=true`, so the manuals are
# stored and checked out verbatim — no text conversion, ever.
#
# Edit the MASTER upstream and re-propagate; never edit a distributed copy in place.
instruction-manuals/** -text

# Asset artwork is verified BYTE-FOR-BYTE.
#
# `deployment/content/assets/**` is the SOURCE asset tree — it belongs to the SELECTED
# DEPLOYMENT — and `public/assets/**` is its mirrored runtime derivative
# (`scripts/sync-runtime-assets.mjs`, `pnpm assets:check`,
# `deployment/tests/unit/asset-taxonomy-mirror.test.ts`). The mirror proof is a SHA-256
# comparison of the two files as they exist on disk, and the favicon contract
# compares the branding mark with the favicon derived from it — so no automatic
# line-ending conversion may rewrite either side. Store source artwork and its
# runtime mirror verbatim.
#
# Both paths must stay listed: a rule for a tree that no longer exists would stop
# protecting the artwork without failing anything visible (FOUNDATION-PAGES-A1D
# moved the source tree from `assets/` to `content/assets/`, and
# FOUNDATION-DEPLOYMENT-ISO-B2B moved that source tree into the deployment capsule;
# `deployment/tests/unit/asset-taxonomy-mirror.test.ts` now asserts that BOTH paths —
# and only the current ones — carry `-text`).
deployment/content/assets/** -text
public/assets/** -text

# `LICENSE` is the CANONICAL Apache License 2.0 text, installed byte-for-byte
# from <https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt> and never paraphrased,
# reformatted or extended (no copyright-holder name is filled in — the canonical
# appendix placeholders stay as published). It is legal evidence as well as
# configuration, so it is stored and checked out verbatim, for the same reason
# the distributed manuals and the artwork are. Do not reflow it.
LICENSE -text
